<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simplifying surds with coefficients and writing surds as a single square root</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> Simplify \({@k@}\sqrt{{@n1@}}\) to the simplest form. <i>(Note: Write <code>6*sqrt(5)</code> to represent \(6\sqrt{5}\).)</i></p>
<p>Simplified form = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> Express \({@p@}\sqrt{{@q@}}\) as a single square root \(\sqrt{m}\). What is the value of \(m\)?</p>
<p>\(m =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a): Simplifying \({@k@}\sqrt{{@n1@}}\)</b><br>
Find the largest perfect-square factor of \({@n1@}\). Since \({@n1@} = {@a_sq@} \times {@b@}\) and \({@a_sq@} = {@a@}^2\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@k@}\sqrt{{@n1@}} = {@k@}\sqrt{{@a_sq@} \times {@b@}} = {@k@} \times \sqrt{{@a_sq@}} \times \sqrt{{@b@}} = {@k@} \times {@a@}\sqrt{{@b@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {@k@}\sqrt{{@n1@}} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Expressing \({@p@}\sqrt{{@q@}}\) as a single square root \(\sqrt{m}\)</b><br>
To move the outside number \({@p@}\) inside the square root, square it first using \(p = \sqrt{p^2}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {@p@}\sqrt{{@q@}} = \sqrt{{@p@}^2} \times \sqrt{{@q@}} = \sqrt{{@p_sq@} \times {@q@}} = \sqrt{{@ta2@}}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ m = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
